<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-coturnix-japonica-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at 22.42 µm on Holocene Coturnix japonica plumage — Code-to-model traceability: 86/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The module docstring states the PDE, the critical-wavenumber formula, and the claim that D_v is a weak lever. lean_scaled_identities repeats the integers proved in Loop_3157. The math-KG yaml points at those declarations. Deduction: there is no line-by-line map onto numbered equations of Prum & Williamson 2002, because that paper's follicle geometry is not the system integrated here." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-coturnix-japonica-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-coturnix-japonica-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-coturnix-japonica-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.6e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-coturnix-japonica-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at 22.42 µm on Holocene Coturnix japonica plumage — Model fidelity to source: 88/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The script integrates Schnakenberg kinetics and the Turing dispersion, including tr J = -0.140, det J = 1, k_c^2 = 3112/259, and an open band. Five Lean theorems check those scaled integers with no sorry. The length unit is fixed so the nominal linear wavelength is 2.242e-5 m. Deduction: the rates are not Harris et al. 2005 biochemical constants, and the saturated spacing is not the linear wavelength." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "models/2026-delphi10000-coturnix-japonica-turing-wavelength-s0.py L16–L22: docstring states the kinetics are phenomenological, not fitted Shh/Bmp2 rates <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc/models/2026-delphi10000-coturnix-japonica-turing-wavelength-s0.py#L16-L22>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-coturnix-japonica-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-coturnix-japonica-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-coturnix-japonica-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at 22.42 µm on Holocene Coturnix japonica plumage — Morphometric validation: 84/100" ;
